Put the new drive in the box with a different SCSI ID, partition the new
disk with disklabel, and use vdump piped through vrestore to copy the
filesystems from the old disk to the new.

If you are use advfs filesystems on your root disk, then remember to use
the -t advfs switch with disklabel.

