boot system via CD-Rom to "system management"

do

dd -if=/dev/rrz0c -of=/dev/rrz1c bs=80b

rrz0c could be your root disk and rrz1c could be your new disk Both disks
have to be identical (e.g. rz29/rz29).

dd makes a binary copy of the systemdisk.

after that swap rz1 to rz0

