 Something I missed on the first followup.  On Compaq UNIX you can
 control whether structure and union fields are naturally aligned or
 packed.  On HP-UX you can't.  I've had trouble getting two programs
 which used the same .h file to declare a struct on HP-UX to agree
 how the data should be aligned.  So if you do read and writes of
 entire structs you may have to re-write it as field-by-field I/O.
 
