OK, This is what we've got so far, anyone else have any comments or
shall I make this a formal rfd and post it?

I thought I should send it to comp.unix.osf.osf1, comp.unix.osf.misc
comp.sys.dec and comp.unix.admin along with the required news related
groups, anyone think of any others that need to be told, perhaps the
alpha-osf-managers@ornl.gov mailing list?

Rationale
Compaq's Tru64 Unix product is among the oldest 64bit unix, yet there is no
obvious and specific place to discuss it, or ask questions regarding it's
use and administration.

The current places where Compaq Tru64 Unix is discussed are not intuitively
named for this purpose, and as a result, new users and admins are confused
as to where to post and either ask in general newsgroups, or not at all.

End Rationale

Charter

The purpose of the group is to provide a place for discussion of issues
relating to owning, operating, managing, administering and  using computer
systems running versions of the operating system now officially called
Compaq Tru64 unix, previously called Digital Unix, previously called
osf1.
It is inappropriate to send binary, html or encoded material.
Job postings are unwelcome.
Adverts if posted at all should be short and of the nature of a pointer to
information about a product rather than complete details, they should be in
direct response to a query and still not be repeated more than once per month.


End Charter


Adam Price








