After reading your question, I'm still unclear about how you're trying to
log in.  Are you running a window manager on your PC (as part of Exceed)
and just opening up a local xterm and then trying to log into the Tru64 system,
or are you trying to get an xdm/dtgreet style login, where the Tru64 system
presents some kind of a graphical login screen to the client?

After knowing that, the big question is, "Are you running Enhanced Security?"
Run

	grep -i security /etc/rc.config

or

	rcmgr get SECURITY

to find out.

If you're trying to do a graphical xdm/dtgreet login and you're running
enhanced security, you'll want to read up on default(4), devassign(4), ttys(4),
and probably authcap(4).  DHCP will undoubtedly complicate the picture.

Tim
