Nikola-

Unfortunately, I don't think that's correct.  useradd completely ignores the
settings for u_lock in the defaults database.  It *does* honor whatever you
set up as the Default template, though (i.e. in root's .sysman/Account_defaults
file).

This is documented in the release notes for recent versions of Tru64, e.g.
4.0F's 4.3.7.4 section.

