Using sysconfigdb is just good practice. If you create a directory like 
"/etc/stanza" and put your changes for each subset in there, you can use
sysconfigdb to merge them into sysconfigtab. This gives you a history of
changes you have made and allows you to remove, or modify, them easily, too.

