john hall wrote:

> Is there a way that I can list all the symbols in shared libraries that
> are linked to from an OSF/DU executable?
>

 The "odump -Dt" command will dump the table of external symbols in a
shared
object,  where a shared object is either a shared library or a -call_shared
linked
executable.

You'll need to run the odump command on each library that the application
links
with to get all the symbols for all libraries.

As of the V5.0 release, you can use the "ldd" command to list the dynamic
library dependencies of an application.  Prior to V5.0,  to get the
dependencies,
you'll need to use "odump -Dl"  on the application and all of its
dependencies.

Joe Mario
Compaq Tru64 UNIX Development Environment




