> Umm, so if I have a 4mm DAT drive, it's:
> 
>         /dev/MAKEDEV "4mm DAT drive" ??
> 
>         Stu

This has already been answered further up, but...

I think typeoftapedevice is more along the lines of the tape/interface
combination, not media the tape uses. For example, most people can get
away with:

	/dev/MAKEDEV tz4

That would create the device special files for a tape (t) device on SCSI
(z) id four (4). This would do for just about any DAT, 8mm, or DLT drive
that had it's SCSI id set to 4 and was connected to the first "regular"
SCSI interface. IDE, HSZ, or other interfaces would probably need
different mnemonics. And it is also my understanding that device names
have TOTALLY changed under Tru64 (DUNIX 5.0??)... For all I know, you
actually use the word "tape" in there somewhere.

