  If you are purchasing new, you will want either the AlphaStation XP900
  or the AlphaServer DS10 -- these are effectively the same system, check
  the licensing and the I/O hardware that is included and/or optional.

  You will want to ensure that the graphics controller chosen is supported
  by both platforms.  (The ELSA GLoria Synergy is the usual choice, though 
  the OpenVMS drivers for the PowerStorm 300 and PowerStorm 350 are expected
  to be available very shortly...)

  If purchasing used, the AlphaStation 255 and AlphaStation 500 are often
  good choices for workstations, as are the various rawhide-derived 
  AlphaServer systems.  (eg: 800, 1200, 4000, 4100 series.  The lattermost 
  supports multiple instances for use in an OpenVMS Galaxy configuration.)
  Check the I/O widgets, and particularly the graphics, for support...

  If you choose the Personal Workstation series or the AlphaStation XP1000
  series, you will have to check the particular configuration carefully for 
  support on both operating systems, as there are some wrinkles involved	
  -- depending on the particular box and the particular flavor and the
  particular bridge chip used, as well as the I/O widgets...

