Jan Lowe (jyl@mrc-lmb.cam.ac.uk) wrote:
: The problem is that psrinfo takes a long time to complete (up to 5s) and is not
: acceptable to have in everyone's .cshrc file. 
: QUESTION: is there another (faster) way of getting the same information about
: the processor(s) ?

'psrinfo -v' spends most of the time reading /var/adm/wtmp; I guess that it that
gets excessively large, you *might* have a relatively long delay here. You can
always rotate /var/adm/wtmp at system reboot, or, you can simply get the answer
you want by doing getsysinfo(GSI_CPU) (see the manual page). All the necessary
defines are in /usr/include/machine/hal/cpuconf.h

Cheers,

/Serge.P

