Hi,

/dev/ttyd0 is a dialer device for the modem, your UPS will require a
"normal" comm port (/dev/tty00).

Use "setup" and reconfigure your modem to work on comm2 (/dev/tty01), don't
forget to remove the config from comm1. You may have to delete /dev/ttyd0
and re-MAKEFILE /dev/tty00

Cunsult the documentation on the UPS for the config of the comm port, you
may have to make changes at console level.

Check out the modem man page for more on modems - experiance has taught me
that they can be tricky.

Hope this helps,

Kev

