upper/lower case, with drive letter A or without, with .exe extension
...

The tape drive doesn't show up in the "show config" output (the
externally connected RAID array does). I added the HP description to the
/etc/db.dbase file and run ddr_config. Do I have to recompile the kernel
and how?

I know, an external DAT drive would have been nicer and probably easier
to install, but because of the connections and the termination of the
RA3000 it seemed much easier this way.

Thanks for any hints, help or pointers to more information.

