Clemens Vonrhein (vonrhein@globalphasing.com) wrote:
: I'm trying to connect an internal DAT tape drive to the internal narrow
: device connection of a KZPBA-CB SCSI controller in a Digital Personal
: Workstation 500au.

Make sure eight upper bits (and ONLY eight upper bits) are actively
terminated on the controlle (at least for KZPBA-CA, this can be controlled
by an SRM variable - unfortunately, I do not have a spare au-series to
test it on at the moment). By default, the whole bus is terminated at
the controller - which is, obviously, not that you want. Decpaq with also 
sell you a terminating adapter, but, given it's price, it's at least worth
trying the built-in terminator ...

Regards,

/Serge.P

