True, but disklabel still insists on a disktab entry on the command
line. If it doesn't find the disktab entry it will use the geometry
from the disk and apply a default label. So if you invoke disklabel
(after setting the SCSI Id of the device to let's say 5) as 
       disklabel -rw rz5c hell_you_wont_find_this_in_disktab
you'll be fine. You may have to do a (cd  /dev; ./MAKEDEV rz5 before,
though).

