The reason why newly created accounts are locked is because account deafults say
so. Either manually edit the file /etc/auth/system/defaults and change
":u_lock:" to ":@u_lock:" or do it in Account Manager -> local templates ->
Default template.

While you are there, you can change expiration and lifetime for accounts, if you
wish.

> Personally, I really wish there were some good command-line enhanced
