>I have a problem with keyboard mapping. I use a PWS600au running DU4.0D
>with an american (LK97W-A2) keyboard. Because of I often need italian
>accented vowels such as:
>
>� � � � � ...
>
>I would like to map some unused keycap-sequence with these letters, for
>example I would like to type Alt-A and get �
>
>I thoroughly read the keyboard(5) man page but I still have no idea how to
>perform such an easy operation, in particular using the xkb (preferred,
>according to the manual page) format.

Try the 

        /usr/bin/X11/dxkeycaps

utility.

It will display a graphic picture of your keyboard, and you can then
play with alternate key mappings and modifier keys.

The utility can then generate an output file that can be feed into
xmodmap during your login so that the keyboard is setup the way you
want each time you log in.



