OK Looking at the file this seems to be the whole charter for the group,
the file mentioned also seems to imply that lots of sites think this group
is bogus and should have been rmgrouped anyway, which troubles me somewhat.

In light of this and the fact that an rfd must have a charter I have started
work on a charter for comp.unix.tru64.
Don't know what to say about adverts, I hate them, but realise that some may
not, so we ought to have a discussion about that before we cast it in stone.
I've written down what I think, and I hope some of you will want to change/
improve on it.

Charter

The purpose of the group is to provide a place for discussion of issues
relating to owning, operating, managing, administering and  using computer
systems running versions of the operating system now officially called
Compaq Tru64 unix, previously called Digital Unix, previously called
osf1.
It is inappropriate to send binary posts (including html).
Job postings are unwelcome.
Adverts if posted at all should be short and of the nature of a pointer to
information about a product rather than complete details, they should not
be repeated more than once per month.

End Charter

Well that's it, doesn't look like much does it, hope it's enough.

Adam Price.






