Brandon Hutchinson wrote in message ...
>Hi,
>
>we bought an Alphasttion XP1000 (DU 4F) before Xmas and it has a cdrom
>drive attached to the IDE port. I cannot figure out how to mount or
>access this device.  The manula assumes cdroms are scsi devices but this
>one is not.
>
>Any ideas on what it should be called eg for MAKEDEV or how to otherwise
>access it?

If it is anything like other Alpha machines with IDE, It's pretending to
be scsi, the first IDE bus pretends to be scsi bus 0, the second pretends
to be scsi bus 1, the master device is scsi id 0 and the slave is id1, so
the cdrom drive will be one of the scsi drives /dev/rz0,dev/rz1,dev/rz7
or /dev/rz8. I'm guessing /dev/rz0.

Hope this helps
Adam







