WB3KUM <d.breeden@nospam.wcom.com> writes:
>Whenever we print through Unix a postscript file on an HP4000 networked
>printer, it selects the legal size paper.  We even have flip/floped the
>paper trays!
>
>I have been unable to see how to select a paper size or paper tray in
>the printcap file.  This is happening with several application so I
>suspect it is a printer set up problem in Unix (works fine in
>Windows/Novell).

Have you checked the Postscript file to see if it is specifying which tray
to use?  That code runs last, so will override any tray settings you do
from the printer console or by commands sent from the queue when the job
is sent to the printer.  If the tray/paper size is set in the Postscript
file, then you will need to change the print setups in the applications
sending the files.  Also check which print driver is selected, the codes
for selecting papertrays vary from printer to printer.  If the one used
does not send codes compatible with the HP4000, the wrong tray may end up
being selected.

Joe Heimann

