> the printcap file.  This is happening with several application so I
> suspect it is a printer set up problem in Unix (works fine in
> Windows/Novell).
> 
> Any and all help is greatly appreciated.

	The HP4000 reads how the paper tray is setup mechanically.  Make
sure that the guides in the tray are set to the correct paper size. 
We just had a very similar problem where a bozo user was trying to
put legal size paper in an HP4000N and all they ended up doing was
moving the guide from "letter" to "A4".  After that every time
someone tried to print it would demand to be feed from the sheet
feeder (tray 1) because it thought it had A4 paper instead of letter
in the paper tray (tray 2).

			Hope this helps,
			      Don


