DEC 3000 is a TurboChannel machine
AlphaServer 800 is a PCI machine
PCI bus is faster and cheaper and more spreadly used than TurboChannel

DEC 3000 has had umpteen various models (few of them with 175MHz).
It is better to know the model number than the frequency.

http://infopad.EECS.Berkeley.EDU/CIC/summary/local/
http://www.specbench.org

The classes of machines (WORKGROUP, DEPARTMENT, ENTERPRISE) are for
licensing issues and not really performance issues. 
A more recent WORKGROUP machine is most likely faster than (any)
earlier ENTERPRISE machine.
So replace (at least every three years) your hardware, if you can.

Consider also (only new, hard to find used ones) DS10/XP900 or DS20/XP1000.

