> I have an application that produces aoutput for a dot matrix printer. Some
> characters have to be replaced before they are sent to the printer. I tried
> to add lines to /etc/printcap (if, of, etc) but could not succeed.
> 
> Does anybody have experience with filters?

Sure.

If the printer is a remote printer, filtering won't work with if/of. The
trick in this case is (or can be) to make two queues, a local fake and
the real remote. Print to the local and let it call a if/of script that
translates the characters, and then at then end prints the result to the
remote queue. It's ugly but it works.
If you need to make a general solution, you can transfer parameters to
the if script using the af option. It's not intended for this use, but
again... it works. It'll show up as paramter $8 in the if script.

If you need an example I can post one. I have a ES40 cluster with about
400 printers configured like this.

I've never quite understood why if/of doesn't work with remote queues,
anyone ?

Will Advanced Printing solve some of these issues ?



